From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] answer the Escape key in the stream window

WaylandVideoSurface::virtualKeyFor translates the key codes the
compositor reports into the virtual keys the host speaks, and it has no
entry for evdev code 1: Escape translated to 0, and
WaylandVideoSurface::submitKey returns at once when the virtual key is 0,
so the press never went out and the menus of Dark and Darker could never
be dismissed. Escape is VK_ESCAPE = 0x1b, the same table the rest of the
physical keys are already in.

Greppable markers: none added; the press shows up in the stream log that
submitKey already writes
---

--- a/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp
+++ b/opennow-qt/src/streaming/rendering/WaylandVideoSurface.cpp
@@ -559,6 +559,7 @@
     // virtual keys the host speaks. The physical keys of a keyboard game are all
     // here; anything else is left alone rather than guessed.
     switch (evdev) {
+    case 1: return 0x1b;   // Escape
     case 2: return 0x31;   // 1
     case 3: return 0x32;   // 2
     case 4: return 0x33;   // 3
